## 2. Service Lifetimes

### Singleton

**One instance for application lifetime**

```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IMaritimeDataService, MaritimeDataService>();
```

**When to Use**:
- Stateless services
- Configuration services
- Caches
- Expensive to create

**Example**:
```csharp
// Same instance returned every time
var service1 = serviceProvider.GetService<IMaritimeDataService>();
var service2 = serviceProvider.GetService<IMaritimeDataService>();
// service1 == service2 (same instance)
```

### Scoped

**One instance per HTTP request (or scope)**

```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<IVesselService, VesselService>();
```

**When to Use**:
- Most services
- Services that need request context
- Services with request-scoped state

**Example**:
```csharp
// Different instance per request
// Request 1: service1
// Request 2: service2
// service1 != service2 (different instances)
```

### Transient

**New instance each time**

```csharp
builder.Services.AddTransient<IUtilityService, UtilityService>();
```

**When to Use**:
- Lightweight services
- Stateless utilities
- Services that should not be shared

**Example**:
```csharp
// New instance each time
var service1 = serviceProvider.GetService<IUtilityService>();
var service2 = serviceProvider.GetService<IUtilityService>();
// service1 != service2 (different instances)
```

