## 4. Constructor Injection

### Preferred Pattern

**Constructor Injection** (recommended):
```csharp
public class VesselService : BaseMaritimeService, IVesselService
{
    private readonly IVesselRepository _repository;
    private readonly ILogger<VesselService> _logger;

    public VesselService(
        IVesselRepository repository,
        ILogger<VesselService> logger)
        : base(logger)
    {
        _repository = repository;
        _logger = logger;
    }
}
```

**Benefits**:
- Dependencies are explicit
- Required dependencies are enforced
- Easy to test (pass mocks)
- Clear dependencies

### Property Injection (Avoid)

**Property Injection** (not recommended):
```csharp
public class VesselService
{
    [Inject]  // ❌ Not recommended
    public IVesselRepository Repository { get; set; }
}
```

**Why Avoid**:
- Dependencies are hidden
- Optional dependencies (can be null)
- Harder to test
- Less explicit

