## 9. Testing with Dependency Injection

### Mocking Dependencies

```csharp
[Fact]
public async Task GetVessel_ReturnsVessel()
{
    // Arrange
    var mockRepository = new Mock<IVesselRepository>();
    mockRepository.Setup(r => r.GetById(1))
        .ReturnsAsync(new Vessel { Id = 1, Name = "Test Vessel" });
    
    var logger = new Mock<ILogger<VesselService>>();
    var service = new VesselService(mockRepository.Object, logger.Object);

    // Act
    var result = await service.GetVesselAsync(1);

    // Assert
    Assert.NotNull(result);
    Assert.Equal("Test Vessel", result.Name);
}
```

**Benefits**:
- Easy to test
- Isolated unit tests
- Fast execution
- Clear test setup

